     "<div dir=\"ltr\">As a follow-up (I still don&#39;t have a solution to this yet), if I remove the hook below and simply knit my document, then I get warnings and errors in fuchsia and red.  However, in the .Tex document there are these definitions:<div><br></div><div><div>\\definecolor{warningcolor}{rgb}{1, 0, 1}</div><div>\\definecolor{errorcolor}{rgb}{1, 0, 0}</div><div><br></div><div>If I change both to 0,0,0 and compile the .Tex document, then the warnings and errors are in black as I want them.  Is there a way to set or define these colors in the .Rnw document?</div></div></div>"
    ],
